// =============================================================================
// core/hash/checksum/mod.vr — corruption detection, NOT security
// =============================================================================
// Layer: 1 (depends on core primitives only)
// =============================================================================
//

// Checksums detect ACCIDENTAL corruption — bit flips on a wire, a
// truncated write, a bad sector. They give no security property at
// all: producing a second input with the same CRC is a linear-algebra
// exercise, not an attack.
//

// Use when the adversary is noise. When the adversary is a person,
// use `core.hash.crypto` (unkeyed) or `core.mac` (keyed).
//

// =============================================================================

module core.hash.checksum;

public module crc32;
public module crc32c;
